    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "In this study, we have demonstrated the ability of Galderia Sulphuraria an acidophilic, thermotolerant, algal species, in removing organic carbon, ammoniacal nitrogen and phosphate from primary settled wastewater. A photosynthetically oxygenated waste to energy recovery (POWER) system utilizing G.sulphuraria was engineered to treat primary settled wastewater and to recover net energy and nutrients. This long term study confirmed that G.sulphuraria was able to grow well in primary-settled wastewater and to reduce the organic carbon (measured as BOD5) level of over 70%, the ammoniacal nitrogen level of over 85% and phosphate level of over 90% in three days. In addition, the system achieved effective removal of inorganic ions and heavy metals such as Fe, As, Se, Al, Ca, Mg, Cr. The system achieved decrease in coliforms counts from 3*10^7 in the primary effluent to non-detectable level in 6 days.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
